{"schema":"LAW_EN_DOCUMENT_V1","id":"i18n-4cd238f3a79c15cb5274492656f57453eb4d7216154486b5","family_id":"KR:000623","country":"KR","language":"en","title":"Traffic, Energy and Environment Tax Act","title_original":"교통ㆍ에너지ㆍ환경세법","kind":"법률","source_version":"276071","promulgated":null,"effective":null,"translation_status":"AI_DRAFT","body_status":"BODY_LOADED","source_url":"https://www.law.go.kr/LSW/lsInfoP.do?lsiSeq=276071","source_sha256":"bcb73bb30b84092164a84d6f85dcf76e19bd67f4f4178be2e290e41bb600bb3b","body_sha256":"0889a6af4adc381f9df594293cfbe03aba94743152185a718f810ef1ded38fbf","article_count":0,"full_text":"Act No. 21065 (October 1, 2025)\nAct Partially Amending the Government Organization Act\n[Main text omitted]\nADDENDA\nArticle 1 (Enforcement date)\nThis Act shall enter into force on the date of its promulgation; provided that, among the Acts amended pursuant to Article 7 of the Addenda, the provisions amending Acts promulgated before the enforcement of this Act but whose enforcement dates have not yet arrived shall enter into force on the respective enforcement dates of those Acts, and the amended provisions specified in the following subparagraphs shall enter into force on the dates specified therein.\n1. The amended provisions in the following items shall enter into force on January 2, 2026; provided that, among the Acts amended pursuant to Article 7 of the Addenda (limited to the portions relating to the amended provisions in items (a) and (b)), the provisions amending Acts promulgated before the enforcement date specified in the main text but whose enforcement dates have not yet arrived by that date shall enter into force on the respective enforcement dates of those Acts.\n    (a) The amended provisions of Articles 19 (4), 23, 29 (1) 1 and 30.\n    (b) The amended provisions of Articles 12 (2), 19 (3), 22 and the proviso to Article 29 (2) (limited to the portions concerning the Minister of Finance and Economy and the Ministry of Finance and Economy).\n    (c) The Acts amended pursuant to Article 7 of the Addenda (limited to the portions relating to the amended provisions in items (a) and (b)).\n2. Omitted.\nArticles 2 through 6 Omitted.\nArticle 7 (Amendment of other Acts)\n(1) through (10) Omitted.\n(11) The Traffic, Energy and Environment Tax Act is partially amended as follows:\nIn Article 14 (2), \"Minister of Economy and Finance\" is replaced by \"Minister of Finance and Economy\".\n(12) through (626) Omitted.\nArticle 8 Omitted.\n\n[Partial Amendment]\nReasons for Amendment\nThe purpose is to disperse and reallocate functions and powers concentrated in particular ministries, thereby addressing concerns about concentration of authority and strengthening the specialized expertise of each function; to redesign the government organizational system so that it can respond actively to changes in the administrative environment, including the climate crisis and the major transition brought about by artificial intelligence; to readjust the deputy prime minister system and the system of ministries under the Prime Minister to strengthen capabilities in science and technology, artificial intelligence, national data and intellectual property administration; and to strengthen government functions so that gender equality policies and occupational safety and health policies can be actively pursued.\n\nMain Contents\n(a) The Broadcasting and Communications Commission is abolished and the Broadcasting, Media and Communications Commission is established. Broadcasting promotion affairs currently performed by the Ministry of Science and ICT are transferred to the Broadcasting, Media and Communications Commission (Articles 2 (2) 1 and 31).\n(b) Two deputy prime ministers are established to oversee and coordinate economic policy and policies on science and technology and artificial intelligence. These positions are held concurrently by the Minister of Finance and Economy and the Minister of Science and ICT, respectively, while the deputy prime minister position held concurrently by the Minister of Education is abolished (Article 19).\n(c) To ensure mutual checks and balances between budgetary and economic functions and strengthen the expertise of each function, the Ministry of Economy and Finance is divided into the Ministry of Planning and Budget under the Prime Minister and the Ministry of Finance and Economy (newly inserted Article 23; Article 30).\n(d) Statistics Korea and the Korean Intellectual Property Office are upgraded respectively to the Ministry of National Data and the Ministry of Intellectual Property under the Prime Minister (newly inserted Articles 27 and 28).\n(e) The order of the executive ministries is adjusted to reflect the reorganization of the deputy prime ministers and executive ministries, and the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment and the Ministry of SMEs and Startups are each to have two vice ministers (Article 29).\n(f) To establish a system enabling mutual checks between investigative and prosecutorial agencies, the Prosecutors' Office is abolished, and a Public Prosecution Office under the Minister of Justice and a Serious Crime Investigation Office under the Minister of the Interior and Safety are established, respectively (Articles 35 and 37).\n(g) The Ministry of Environment is reorganized as the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment, and energy affairs formerly assigned to the Ministry of Trade, Industry and Energy (excluding the nuclear power export sector) are transferred to the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment so that environmental, climate change and energy policies can be pursued in a coordinated and integrated manner. To reflect the transfer of energy affairs, the Ministry of Trade, Industry and Energy is reorganized as the Ministry of Trade and Industry (Articles 41 and 43).\n(h) The Ministry of Employment and Labor is to have one headquarters chief responsible for occupational safety and health affairs, who is to be a political-service official (newly inserted Article 44 (2)).\n(i) To pursue gender equality policies comprehensively, the Ministry of Women and Family is renamed the Ministry of Gender Equality and Family and is expanded and reorganized, including through the transfer of certain related affairs from the Ministry of Employment and Labor (Article 45; Article 2 (1) of the Addenda).\n\n<Provided by the Ministry of Government Legislation>\n","metadata":{"author_method":"Exact held-source units translated or completed using explicitly recorded source/target spans; original official records remain unchanged. All new units are MACHINE_TRANSLATION and UNREVIEWED.","author_source_review_evidence":[{"evidence":{"exact_author_input":{"path":"D:\\lawsofkorea\\projece\\07_법률번역\\06_법령별다국어완성\\LAW12_20261018_1442\\workc_1129_2094\\review_pending\\WORKC_G01_P04\\1526_KR000623\\translations\\author_inputs\\1fd6367ab263d6f8766c58fa9647fb8cec0c16a95e3059ed31442bfffffea6ae.ascii.json","sha256":"1fd6367ab263d6f8766c58fa9647fb8cec0c16a95e3059ed31442bfffffea6ae"},"protocol":"WORKC_P04_1526_EXPLICIT_SOURCE_REVIEWED_AUTHOR_INPUT_V1","reviewed_source_units":[{"source_component_text_sha256":"01a958251b66d49e6ef851a24902b0d8ab03eb9f953aff413c61f6671e0dfe77","unit_key":"amendment-text"},{"source_component_text_sha256":"ad0d0e477006b39082fddbaff47acfd45a94bbedf3d3b10391915e764335144b","unit_key":"enactment-amendment-reason"}],"source_component_text_sha256":"01a958251b66d49e6ef851a24902b0d8ab03eb9f953aff413c61f6671e0dfe77","source_law_id":"kr-000623-276071-ko","source_review_complete":true,"source_xml_sha256":"bcb73bb30b84092164a84d6f85dcf76e19bd67f4f4178be2e290e41bb600bb3b","target_body_sha256":"2b73739925cb4a408c8612f293a1f07d434234277c4e02caf813c97079d8ead2","unit_key":"amendment-text"},"unit_key":"amendment-text"},{"evidence":{"exact_author_input":{"path":"D:\\lawsofkorea\\projece\\07_법률번역\\06_법령별다국어완성\\LAW12_20261018_1442\\workc_1129_2094\\review_pending\\WORKC_G01_P04\\1526_KR000623\\translations